    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0629" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E.W./9–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-06T15:00:00+03:00">September 6,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 7—2:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3342. Molotov has given the British Ambassador and myself a draft of peace terms
                    for Finland. He has invited the British Ambassador and myself to discuss them
                    this evening. I agreed to attend with the understanding that I would be present
                    as an observer.</p>
                <pb facs="0630" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/>
                <p>Molotov asked the British Ambassador to inform his Government in its
                    consideration of the Rumanian reparations<anchor n="74" xml:id="d555-f1"/> that
                    the Soviet Government was now proposing to reduce its reparation demands on
                    Finland from $600,000,000 to $300,000,000.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d555-f1" n="74" xml:id="d555-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence relating to the Soviet and Allied conditions for an armistice
                    with Rumania, see <ref target="frus1944v04">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >iv</hi>
                    </ref>, section under Rumania entitled “Negotiations leading to signing of
                    armistice with Rumania …”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
